  "behavior": [
    "Public reset_allocator, add_index, remove_index, inspect_index, iterate_add_indices, iterate_remove_indices, iterate_inspect_indices adapt the seven protected methods without exposing mutable map keys or raw Cell graph ownership.",
    "Index slices borrow caller coordinates. Canonical CellMap uses shared heterogeneous bucket traversal directly on borrowed slices; add creates the native lookup Cell copy after growth, including hits, without an extra temporary owned CellIndex.",
    "A shared recursive walker changes axes zero through signed idim, axis zero fastest, preserves later caller coordinates, and leaves the cursor at its native final position. Partial axes do not depend on the public filter dimension or index length matching the size array.",
    "Reversed outer ranges return before touching the cursor, including an empty cursor. Reversed inner ranges still allow outer coordinates to reach their upper endpoints. INT_MIN/INT_MAX singleton ranges terminate without overflow.",
    "Clone, target-equality and inspection callback failures retain earlier insertions/removals/purges and stop with the caller cursor at the current cell. Existing canonical target allocation/destructor/unlink phases are reused unchanged.",
    "reset_allocator publishes/adopts arenas through the existing canonical reset path and preserves cell sizes and dimension. Existing point APIs share the same graph and core retain traversal."
  ],
