  "adaptations_and_remaining_gaps": [
    "Slices represent borrowed CellIndex/Cell.index arguments, so native Cell object identity, retained raw pointers and arbitrary aliasing between cursor and min/max are not exposed. Rust exclusive cursor borrowing excludes native caller alias patterns.",
    "Negative idim or reached out-of-bounds slice access returns Failure before mutation rather than native undefined access. A reversed outer range remains a successful no-op even when cursor storage is empty.",
    "The existing coordinate-range APIs retain their CellIndices implementation and zero-dimensional/clamping extensions; these new explicit helpers use native signed-axis semantics over provided index slices.",
    "Protected Cell constructors, IsEqual/operator==, CellHasher callable wrapper and native move construction/assignment remain separate callable-surface work. In particular move assignment may overwrite a live target head; no closure is claimed for it.",
    "Existing CellIndex SmallVec48 versus native56 bytes, Cell56 versus64, and MapNode<Cell>64 versus72 remain open layout/allocation-byte gaps. No LocalArray source or arbitrary padding was changed.",
    "Existing documented Rust Drop-unwind recovery, allocator extensions, generic payload ABI/address-sensitive operations, and concurrent/reentrant whole-owner observations remain outside this bounded proof.",
    "Scoped source snapshots include relevant prior CellFilter/map dependencies and current tests; they are not whole-workspace compiler closure or a replacement for the global declaration inventory."
  ]
